  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Building the capacities of procurement institutions to achieve development outcomes</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Component A: Strengthening the Procurement Directorate of Ministry of Finance through: (a) assessment of the effectiveness of present public procurement system; (b) development of approrpiate laws, rules and regulations; and ( c) development of a set of compliance and performance indicators; Component B: Capacity building on procurement by (a) conduct of training needs analysis; (b) training and workshop including participation in study tours; and (c) formulate the national training program. To strengthen the procurement legal system, improve monitoring, and enhance the capacities of the National Procurement Directorate (NPD) and procuring entities to improve procurement implementation. The legal and regulatory framework will be strengthened by the passage of an omnibus procurement law.  The improvement in monitoring will be achieved through the development and implementation of agency procurement performance evaluation system.  The capacities of the NPD and procuring entities will be strengthened through the development and delivery of a national training program on the new procurement system, its documents and tools.</narrative>
  </description>
